BUG: the solution doc's suggested way to verify run_apps.sh cannot work as written
File: docs/solutions/NEARS-1689-qa-lock-liveness.md (lines 235-238)
Severity: low | breaks_ac: false | surface: docs (shipped by this change)

The doc offers two ways to handle the run_apps.sh residual:

  237  worktree exercises the **primary tree's unfixed** guard and will look unchanged. Verify `run_apps.sh` by
  238  pointing `LOCK_GUARD` at the worktree copy, or accept it as verifiable only post-merge, and say which was

The first option is not achievable without editing the file. run_apps.sh assigns both
variables unconditionally -- neither honours a pre-set environment value:

  scripts/run_apps.sh:5    ROOT_DIR="/Users/Apple/Projects/nears"
  scripts/run_apps.sh:14   LOCK_GUARD="$ROOT_DIR/scripts/qa-lock-guard.sh"

Contrast the same file's overridable vars, which use the ${VAR:-default} form:

  scripts/run_apps.sh:10   FLUTTER_BIN="${FLUTTER_BIN:-/Users/Apple/Tools/flutter/bin/flutter}"
  scripts/run_apps.sh:11   ADB_BIN="${ADB_BIN:-$SDK_ROOT/platform-tools/adb}"

So `LOCK_GUARD=... bash scripts/run_apps.sh` is silently overwritten at line 14 and the
primary tree's guard is sourced anyway.

Impact: a future verifier following the doc's first option would believe they had
exercised the worktree guard when they had not -- a false green, in a ticket about
false greens. The doc's SECOND option ("accept it as verifiable only post-merge") is
correct and is the path this QA run took, so nothing was mis-verified here.

Suggested fix (engineer's call): either drop the first option from the doc, or make the
two vars overridable -- ROOT_DIR="${ROOT_DIR:-/Users/Apple/Projects/nears}" and
LOCK_GUARD="${LOCK_GUARD:-$ROOT_DIR/scripts/qa-lock-guard.sh}" -- which would also make
the residual verifiable pre-merge.

